in @prism
in @meta

# @glass — the floor of the substrate's self-conversation.
#
# Declares the types of the glass wall (the substrate-altitude loss
# carrier and verdict surface), the universal content-addressed atom
# (`splinter`), the SpectralUuid-addressed settled composition
# (`shard`), and the `glass` keyword for declaring sub-prisms inside
# a parent prism.
#
# === The three-layer recognition (2026-06-06, Alex + Reed → Mara) ===
#
# Alex's naming: "The `splinter` is the content addressed fragment.
# And the `shard` is a settlement of content addressed splinters into
# SpectralUuid addressed stored fragment. The bottom and the top
# meeting in the middle. This is the load-bearing bridge for
# everything that follows."
#
# Three layers emerge:
#
#   splinter (BOTTOM)     — the oid-addressed content atom at every
#                            altitude. The universal carrier of content.
#                            { content: oid, altitude: ref,
#                              transparency: transparency(altitude) }.
#                            What Fate emits a proposed composition of.
#
#   shard (MIDDLE)        — the SpectralUuid-addressed settlement of
#                            composed splinters into a stored fragment.
#                            What `settle` produces; what `@mirror/store`
#                            keeps; what `peer.eigenboard` types as
#                            (per boot/std/peer.mirror).
#                            { id: SpectralUuid, splinters: [splinter],
#                              transparency: transparency(altitude) }.
#
#   SpectralUuid (TOP)    — the graph-navigatable spectral identifier.
#                            128 bits, golden-ratio split: 48 ACTIVE
#                            (quantized SpectralCoordinate<5>; leading;
#                            navigable) + 80 DARK (BLAKE3-truncated
#                            content hash; trailing; identity). Realized
#                            in prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs;
#                            declared at the substrate altitude when
#                            the shard altitude lands (see deferred
#                            note below the shard declaration).
#
# Bottom (splinter, atomic content) and top (SpectralUuid, spectral
# identity) MEET IN THE MIDDLE at shard (the settled, stored, navigable
# unit). au is the proposed shard (Fate-emitted splinters,
# uncommitted); settle is the act that composes splinters through the
# property chain into a shard (SpectralUuid-addressed, stored).
#
# The transition:
#
#   au (Fate-emitted splinters, uncommitted)
#      ↓ settle (property-chain run; verify; commit)
#   Imperfect<shard> (SpectralUuid-identified, stored)
#
# Spec: docs/specs/transparency.md, docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md
#       (the bottom-top-middle recognition section).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (SpectralUuid as
#                      monoid homomorphism w.r.t. shard merge).
#
# Per prism-as-trait-as-everything: `prism @glass { ... }` declares
# @glass IS a prism. No `<= prism` redundancy. The five-op block
# below is the canonical declaration form (cf. boot/00-prism.mirror).

prism @glass {
  focus glass
  project glass
  split glass
  shift glass
  settle glass
}

# `glass` keyword — sub-prism declaration form inside a parent prism.
#
# Surface: `glass @<name> { <body> }` declares a sub-prism scoped to
# the enclosing prism. Abstract here so the parser knows what the
# `glass` token means structurally; the obligation block (\) is
# discharged downstream when concrete sub-prisms land.
glass(name) -> prism { \ }

# === types of the glass wall ===

# location — where in the substrate an opacity was observed.
# `file: ref` is the canonical substrate file reference (per
# boot/01a-error.mirror's location precedent).
type location = {
  file: ref,
  span: (u32, u32),
}

# opacity — the minimal located fact. One smudge on the glass.
# property is @nl (human-readable description of what was checked);
# weight is bits-of-missing-information at this site (Shannon-like).
type opacity = {
  location: location,
  property: @nl,
  weight: f64,
}

# opacity_map — the accumulated opacity sites for a transparency.
type opacity_map = [opacity]

# imperfect(a, e, l) — the substrate's three-state outcome functor.
# Re-declared here at the glass altitude to make the loss-carrier
# slot `l` substrate-visible. boot/01a-error.mirror's @imperfect
# parameterizes on (value, loss, error); this is the floor form.
type imperfect(a, e, l) =
  | success(a)
  | partial(a, l)
  | failure(e, l)

# transparency(p) — located opacity over property p. The substrate's
# loss carrier. Replaces the dead MirrorLoss scalar.
type transparency(p) =
  | success
  | partial(opacity_map)
  | failure(opacity_map)

# verdict — the glass-wall verdict surface. Per the spec:
# pass | partial(confidence) | failure(reason). NB: distinct from
# @epistemologic/property's `verdict` (pass | fail(diagnostic) |
# partial(f64, [diagnostic])). See open questions below.
type confidence = f64
type reason = @nl

type verdict =
  | pass
  | partial(confidence)
  | failure(reason)

# property_verdict — a verdict located at a glass-wall site.
type property_verdict = {
  verdict: verdict,
  where: location,
}

# === splinter — the universal content-addressed atom (BOTTOM) ===
#
# A splinter is the substrate's universal content-addressed carrier
# at every altitude. AST nodes are splinters. Targets are splinters.
# Specs are splinters. au is a composition of splinters (proposed;
# pre-commitment). The universe @mirror/mosaic acts on is the
# manifold of splinters at every altitude.
#
# Three structural shapes the splinter takes — realized in the Rust
# substrate as `Fractal::{Shard, Branch, Lens}` (per
# fragmentation/src/fragment.rs; the Rust `Shard` variant name is
# the legacy form for "leaf splinter" and predates Alex's recognition
# that `shard` is the MIDDLE layer — see the deferred Rust-rename
# note below `splinter_shape`):
#
#   atom    — terminal splinter. Leaf. No children. Carries content.
#   fractal — composite splinter. Branch. Carries content + children.
#             The recursive shape. The substrate is self-similar.
#   lens    — referring splinter. Carries content + external targets
#             (by oid). Edges, not containment. Cross-altitude link.
#
# The three shapes are exhaustive. A splinter is one of them. There
# is no fourth shape; per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
# the algebra is closed, and the structural-shape algebra of
# splinters closes at three (terminal / composite / referring).
#
# Identity contract: a splinter's identity IS its content-address.
# Two splinters with byte-equal (content, children-oids-or-targets)
# have the same oid and ARE the same splinter. Per
# [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]] and
# shards/mirror/store.mirror.
#
# Altitude: a splinter lives at an altitude — a substrate ref naming
# where in the prism manifold it sits. `@code/rust`, `@mirror/spec`,
# `@meta/ast`, `@release`, `@ci/github` are all altitudes a splinter
# can be observed at. Cross-altitude composition is shift on
# splinters (per [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]: shift is the
# basis-transformation verb; same content, different declared shape).
#
# Transparency: a splinter carries residual opacity from the
# operations that produced it. transparency<p> is parametric on a
# property; a clean splinter has success; a partial one carries an
# opacity_map naming where the settle was incomplete.
#
# Compare au (shards/mirror/au.mirror): au is Fate-emitted splinters
# (a proposed composition; uncommitted; the property chain has not
# yet been run). settle composes au's splinters through the property
# chain into a shard (SpectralUuid-addressed; stored). au's record
# shape is byte-identical to splinter at the carrier level; the
# distinction is lifecycle position. shard is the settlement target;
# splinter is the atomic unit composed.
#
# Per docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md §2.3 (upserted 2026-06-06):
# au is what Fate emits; shard is what @mirror/store keeps; settle is
# the Kleisli arrow `au → Imperfect<shard>` in the Imperfect monad
# declared above (lines 62-66). The substrate-pull-realize lift of
# `content: oid` to `content: SpectralUuid` resolves at the shard
# layer (shard.id IS SpectralUuid by construction; see the shard
# declaration below). Splinter's `content: oid` stays as it is — the
# atomic content addressing.
#
# Cite: docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md §2 makes this load-bearing.
type splinter(altitude) = {
  content: oid,
  altitude: ref,
  transparency: transparency(altitude),
}

# The three structural shapes a splinter takes. Re-declared at the
# glass altitude so the type system can name them as the disjunctive
# decomposition of `splinter`. The bodies are abstract — the Rust
# substrate (fragmentation/src/fragment.rs) realizes them as
# `Fractal::Shard`, `Fractal::Branch`, `Fractal::Lens`.
#
# Note on the Rust `Fractal::Shard` variant name: the variant predates
# Alex's 2026-06-06 recognition that `shard` is the MIDDLE layer
# (SpectralUuid-addressed settled composition), not the terminal-leaf
# shape. The substrate-side variant is named `atom` to avoid the
# collision; the Rust rename `Fractal::Shard → Fractal::Atom` is a
# deferred substrate-pull-realize tick (see
# docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md, ambiguities section).
type splinter_shape =
  | atom                # terminal; no children
  | fractal([oid])      # composite; child oids
  | lens([oid])         # referring; target oids

# === shard — the SpectralUuid-addressed settled composition (MIDDLE) ===
#
# A shard is what `settle` produces: a SpectralUuid-identified
# composition of splinters that has been verified through the
# property chain and committed to @mirror/store. The bottom (splinter)
# and the top (SpectralUuid) meet in the middle at shard.
#
# Identity contract: a shard's identity IS its SpectralUuid. The
# SpectralUuid is computed from the composed splinter set's monoid-
# homomorphism reduction (per [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] §3 and
# prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs's `from_parts`):
#
#   SpectralUuid(merge(s_1, s_2, ...)) =
#     combine(SpectralUuid(s_1), SpectralUuid(s_2), ...)
#
# The active 48 bits carry the quantized SpectralCoordinate<5>
# (navigable; the local Laplacian neighbourhood structure across the
# composed splinters). The dark 80 bits carry the BLAKE3-truncated
# content hash of the composition (identity; what the splinter set
# hashes to). Both halves compose homomorphically under shard merge.
#
# Settlement contract: a shard EXISTS only as the post-settlement
# form. Pre-settlement, the would-be shard is an au (proposed
# splinters; transparency may be non-zero; not yet committed). The
# property chain (`@epistemologic/property/reflect` per
# boot/std/epistemologic/property.mirror) runs through every property
# at the declared altitude; the verdict lifts into Imperfect:
#
#   pass     — shard committed; transparency = success.
#   partial  — shard committed with located transparency; the
#              opacity_map names what could not be settled; kintsugi
#              re-reads to pick the next focus.
#   failure  — au stays in Fate's buffer; no shard committed.
#
# Where shard already lives in the substrate:
#
#   - boot/std/peer.mirror declares `eigenboard: shard` (the typed
#     handle to the peer's current spectral state). The peer.eigenboard
#     IS a SpectralUuid-addressed shard whose splinters carry the
#     peer's current tensions / gestalt / identity.
#   - fragmentation/src/shard_ref.rs realizes shard's typed handle
#     as `ShardRef { id: SpectralUuid, context: ShardContext,
#     budget_bytes: BudgetBytes }`. The substrate names what the
#     algebra IS; the Rust crate names how the shape is implemented.
#   - shards/mirror/store.mirror declares `type shard_ref = oid` —
#     this becomes structurally a SpectralUuid (the lift §9.7 of
#     mosaic-as-type-system.md anticipates resolves naturally here:
#     `shard.id IS SpectralUuid by construction`).
#
# The substrate-pull-realize lift to `id: SpectralUuid` is captured
# below as a deferred tick: SpectralUuid is currently a Rust-only
# type (prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs). When SpectralUuid lands at
# the substrate altitude (likely in `shards/mirror/spectral_uuid.mirror`
# or under `@mirror/store`), this field's type tightens from `oid` to
# `SpectralUuid`. Until then, the substrate names what shard IS; the
# property chain enforces SpectralUuid validity at commit time.
#
# Cite: docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md (the bottom-top-middle
# recognition section, upserted 2026-06-06).
type shard(altitude) = {
  id: oid,                          # → SpectralUuid when declared at substrate (deferred lift)
  splinters: [splinter(altitude)],
  transparency: transparency(altitude),
}

out @glass
out glass
out location
out opacity
out opacity_map
out imperfect
out transparency
out verdict
out confidence
out reason
out property_verdict
out splinter
out splinter_shape
out shard
